/-
# r107a: Substrate UHF completion — the SPECTRAL BUMP brick toward
#        trace-detection of ideals (and the precise WALL MAP)

★ 2026-07-22 r107a — the first brick toward discharging the r106
completion-tier faithfulness hypothesis
`SubstrateCompletionTraceDetectsIdeals` (r106.s):

    ∀ I : TwoSidedIdeal TimelessFieldCompletion, I ≠ ⊥ →
      ∃ x ∈ I, UHF_trace x ≠ 0

using ONLY what mathlib's CONTINUOUS functional calculus (`cfc`/`cfcₙ`)
can actually reach at this pin (mathlib `eed770a4`, `v4.24.0-rc1`), and
mapping the exact wall where the classical (spectral-projection) route
leaves mathlib's reach. ★

## The framework-first content

r106 built the completion-tier unitary averaging engine and proved,
UNCONDITIONALLY, the non-circular reduction

  `ideal_trace_ne_zero_forces_top` :
     x ∈ I → UHF_trace x ≠ 0 → I = ⊤

so that completion simplicity (hence faithfulness of τ_UHF) follows the
moment one exhibits, inside every nonzero two-sided ideal, an element of
nonzero trace. The classical operator-algebra route to that witness is:

  (α) pick `0 ≠ b ∈ I`; then `a := star b · b ∈ I` is a nonzero
      POSITIVE element;
  (β) apply the DISCONTINUOUS spectral indicator `1_{[‖a‖/2,∞)}` to `a`
      (a spectral PROJECTION `q`), which is a nonzero projection with
      `q ≤ (2/‖a‖)·a`, hence `q` lies in the (closed) ideal generated by
      `a`, and `τ_UHF(q) > 0`.

r107a executes as much of this as mathlib's CONTINUOUS calculus permits
and pins the exact obstruction.

**PRIORITY 1 — the reachable `a`-side facts (all UNCONDITIONAL):**

  * `isSelfAdjoint_star_mul_self`, `star_mul_self_ne_zero`,
    `star_mul_self_mem` — `star b · b` is selfadjoint, nonzero when
    `b ≠ 0` (C*-identity `‖star b · b‖ = ‖b‖²`), and stays in any ideal
    containing `b`.
  * `exists_selfAdjoint_ne_zero_mem_of_ne_bot` — step (α), fully proved:
    every nonzero two-sided ideal contains a nonzero selfadjoint
    (indeed `star b · b`) element.
  * `norm_or_neg_norm_mem_spectrum_of_isSelfAdjoint` — for selfadjoint
    `a`, `‖a‖ ∈ σ_ℝ(a) ∨ -‖a‖ ∈ σ_ℝ(a)` (`CStarAlgebra.norm_or_neg…`),
    and the ORDER-conditional `norm_mem_spectrum_of_nonneg_of_...`
    (`CStarAlgebra.norm_mem_spectrum_of_nonneg`) recorded generically
    (see the WALL MAP note on why it is not instantiated at `T∞`).

**PRIORITY 2 — the CONTINUOUS spectral bump (all UNCONDITIONAL):**

  * `spectralBumpFn r t := max 0 (|t| − r)` — a concrete CONTINUOUS,
    nonnegative bump with `g_r(0) = 0` (for `r ≥ 0`) and
    `g_r(±s) = s − r` for `0 ≤ r ≤ s`. This is the continuous
    replacement for the discontinuous spectral indicator of step (β).
  * `spectralBump r a := cfcₙ (spectralBumpFn r) a` — the non-unital
    continuous functional calculus of the bump; selfadjoint
    (`spectralBump_isSelfAdjoint`).
  * **`norm_spectralBump_ge`** / **`spectralBump_ne_zero`** — the genuine
    reachable heart: for nonzero selfadjoint `a`,
    `‖a‖/2 ≤ ‖spectralBump (‖a‖/2) a‖`, so `spectralBump (‖a‖/2) a ≠ 0`.
    Proof: `‖a‖` or `−‖a‖` is a spectrum point where `g` takes value
    `‖a‖/2 > 0`; `norm_apply_le_norm_cfcₙ` (isometry of the non-unital
    cfc) lower-bounds the norm. This is Glimm's "cut near the top of the
    spectrum" step, done CONTINUOUSLY.

**PRIORITY 3 — the honest reduction + the two named links:**

  * `completion_simple_of_bump_links` / `traceDetects_of_bump_links` —
    the r106 engine closes simplicity/trace-detection AS SOON AS the
    bump element (i) lies in the ideal and (ii) has nonzero trace. Both
    are stated as explicit hypotheses; they are exactly the mathlib
    wall (see below).

## ★ THE WALL MAP ★ (primary deliverable)

The reachable chain stops at a nonzero, selfadjoint, CONTINUOUS spectral
bump `p := spectralBump (‖a‖/2) a` obtained from a nonzero positive
`a ∈ I`. To feed the r106 engine we need `p ∈ I` and `τ_UHF(p) ≠ 0`.
Neither is reachable, for TWO independent, precisely-locatable reasons.

**WALL A — the algebraic-vs-closed ideal gap (blocks `p ∈ I`).**
mathlib's `TwoSidedIdeal` is a PURELY ALGEBRAIC ideal (no topology in
its definition). `p = cfcₙ g a` is, by construction, a NORM-LIMIT of
polynomials in `a` without constant term — i.e. of elements
`a·q(a) ∈ I` — but the limit itself lies only in the CLOSURE `Ī`, not
in the algebraic `I`. Concretely the missing declarations are:
  (A1) a topological-closure operation `TwoSidedIdeal.closure` returning
       a `TwoSidedIdeal` (closedness of the closure of a two-sided ideal
       in a topological ring), and
  (A2) a lemma `cfcₙ f a ∈ <closed ideal generated by a>` (equivalently:
       the range of `cfcₙHom` restricted to functions vanishing at `0`
       lies in the closed non-unital ideal generated by `a`).
  NEITHER exists at this pin. mathlib has `cfcₙHom`, its continuity and
  isometry, and the non-unital elemental *subalgebra* generated by `a`,
  but NO API relating `cfcₙ f a` to any (algebraic OR closed) two-sided
  IDEAL. Search of `Mathlib/Analysis/CStarAlgebra/**` and
  `Mathlib/RingTheory/TwoSidedIdeal/**` at `eed770a4` returns:
  `grep cfcₙ ... | grep -i ideal` → ∅; no `TwoSidedIdeal.closure`.
  Bridging A1+A2 also needs the (also-absent) fact that for a UNITAL
  C*-algebra the minimal dense two-sided ideal is the whole algebra
  (the unital Pedersen-ideal theorem `K(A) = A`), which is what makes
  the completion ALGEBRAICALLY (not just topologically) simple — the
  form in which `SubstrateCompletionTraceDetectsIdeals` is stated.

**WALL B — the trace lower bound on the detected element
(blocks `τ_UHF(p) ≠ 0`).**
Even granting `p ∈ I` with `p ≥ 0`, `p ≠ 0`, deducing `τ_UHF(p) ≠ 0`
is EXACTLY faithfulness of `τ_UHF` on positive elements — the very
theorem being pursued — so this route is CIRCULAR unless one imports
deeper structure. The classical non-circular escape replaces the
CONTINUOUS bump `p` by the DISCONTINUOUS spectral PROJECTION
`q = 1_{[‖a‖/2,∞)}(a)` and proves `τ_UHF(q) > 0` from the UHF
trace-scaling / comparison-of-projections theory (every nonzero
projection dominates a matrix unit of some finite level, whose
normalized trace is `> 0`). The missing declarations are:
  (B1) DISCONTINUOUS / indicator continuous functional calculus,
       i.e. a `spectralProjection`/`cfc` for indicator functions of
       clopen spectral sets — mathlib has only `cfc`/`cfcₙ` for
       CONTINUOUS functions; there is no `spectralProjection` and no
       Borel/`cfcₙ`-for-`stepFunction` API;
  (B2) the HEREDITARY-SUBALGEBRA / CORNER API and Murray–von Neumann
       COMPARISON of projections (`p ≾ q`, `qAq`), from which the
       trace lower bound `τ(q) > 0` for a nonzero projection `q` is
       obtained — mathlib has neither hereditary subalgebras/corners
       nor a comparison-of-projections theory for C*-algebras;
  (B3) equivalently, the trace-scaling statement `τ_UHF(q) ≥ 3^{-k}`
       for a nonzero projection `q` at level `k`, which needs (B1)+(B2).

**Classification.** The blocker is BOTH (a) spectral projection =
indicator cfc (discontinuous) — WALL B, part B1 — AND (b) hereditary
subalgebra / corner + comparison of projections — WALL B, parts B2/B3 —
AND, upstream of both and specific to the ALGEBRAIC phrasing of the
hypothesis, (A) the closed-ideal / Pedersen-ideal gap — WALL A. No
embryonic form of `spectralProjection`, `TwoSidedIdeal.closure`,
hereditary subalgebras, or projection comparison exists at this mathlib
pin. r107a is therefore an HONEST partial brick: it discharges the
`a`-side (step α, fully) and the CONTINUOUS spectral cut (step β, up to
the projection), and isolates WALL A and WALL B as the two named links.

Kernel-only [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]. Zero project
axioms. Zero sorries. ONE new file; no existing files modified.

Stage 2026-07-22 r107a — the substrate continuous spectral bump and the
precise two-wall map for completion-tier trace-detection.
-/

import PF.SubstrateCompletionSimplicity
import Mathlib.Analysis.CStarAlgebra.ContinuousFunctionalCalculus.NonUnital
import Mathlib.Analysis.CStarAlgebra.ContinuousFunctionalCalculus.Isometric
import Mathlib.Analysis.CStarAlgebra.ContinuousFunctionalCalculus.Order
import Mathlib.Analysis.CStarAlgebra.ContinuousFunctionalCalculus.Instances
import Mathlib.RingTheory.TwoSidedIdeal.Lattice
import Mathlib.Tactic

namespace PrincipiaTractalis
namespace SubstrateSpectralBump

open scoped ComplexOrder
open SubstrateTimelessFieldCompletion
open SubstrateUHFBoundedTrace
open SubstrateUHFPreTraceDirectLimit
open SubstrateCompletionSimplicity

/-! ## §1 — PRIORITY 1: the reachable `a`-side facts -/

/-- **r107a.1: `star b · b` is selfadjoint.** -/
theorem isSelfAdjoint_star_mul_self (b : TimelessFieldCompletion) :
    IsSelfAdjoint (star b * b) :=
  IsSelfAdjoint.star_mul_self b

/-- **r107a.2: `star b · b ≠ 0` whenever `b ≠ 0`** — the C*-identity
    `‖star b · b‖ = ‖b‖·‖b‖` forces nonvanishing. -/
theorem star_mul_self_ne_zero {b : TimelessFieldCompletion} (hb : b ≠ 0) :
    star b * b ≠ 0 := by
  have hnb : ‖b‖ ≠ 0 := norm_ne_zero_iff.mpr hb
  have hid : ‖star b * b‖ = ‖b‖ * ‖b‖ := CStarRing.norm_star_mul_self
  intro h
  rw [h, norm_zero] at hid
  exact (mul_ne_zero hnb hnb) hid.symm

/-- **r107a.3: any two-sided ideal containing `b` contains `star b · b`.** -/
theorem star_mul_self_mem {I : TwoSidedIdeal TimelessFieldCompletion}
    {b : TimelessFieldCompletion} (hb : b ∈ I) : star b * b ∈ I :=
  I.mul_mem_left _ _ hb

/-- **r107a.4: a nonzero two-sided ideal contains a nonzero element.** -/
theorem exists_ne_zero_mem_of_ne_bot
    (I : TwoSidedIdeal TimelessFieldCompletion) (hI : I ≠ ⊥) :
    ∃ b, b ∈ I ∧ b ≠ 0 := by
  by_contra hcon
  push_neg at hcon
  apply hI
  refine le_antisymm (fun x hx => ?_) bot_le
  rw [TwoSidedIdeal.mem_bot]
  exact hcon x hx

/-- **★ r107a.5: step (α) — every nonzero two-sided ideal contains a
    NONZERO SELFADJOINT (indeed `star b · b`, hence positive) element. ★**
    Fully proved; the reachable half of trace-detection. -/
theorem exists_selfAdjoint_ne_zero_mem_of_ne_bot
    (I : TwoSidedIdeal TimelessFieldCompletion) (hI : I ≠ ⊥) :
    ∃ a, IsSelfAdjoint a ∧ a ≠ 0 ∧ a ∈ I := by
  obtain ⟨b, hbI, hb0⟩ := exists_ne_zero_mem_of_ne_bot I hI
  exact ⟨star b * b, isSelfAdjoint_star_mul_self b, star_mul_self_ne_zero hb0,
    star_mul_self_mem hbI⟩

/-- **r107a.6′ (deliverable 1a, generic): `a ≥ 0` nonzero ⇒
    `‖a‖ ∈ σ_ℝ(a)`.** Recorded generically over any nontrivial C*-algebra
    equipped with the spectral order; NOT instantiated at
    `TimelessFieldCompletion` because the completion carries NO
    `StarOrderedRing` instance at this development stage (the C*-order is
    `CStarAlgebra.spectralOrder`, a `def`, not a registered instance — so
    `0 ≤ (a : T∞)` does not even typecheck without installing it). This is
    a minor upstream wrinkle, orthogonal to WALLS A/B. -/
theorem norm_mem_spectrum_of_nonneg_generic
    {A : Type*} [CStarAlgebra A] [Nontrivial A] [PartialOrder A]
    [StarOrderedRing A] {a : A} (ha : 0 ≤ a) : ‖a‖ ∈ spectrum ℝ a :=
  CStarAlgebra.norm_mem_spectrum_of_nonneg ha

/-! ## §2 — PRIORITY 2: the concrete CONTINUOUS spectral bump -/

/-- **r107a.7: the concrete symmetric continuous spectral bump**
    `g_r(t) = max 0 (|t| − r)`. The CONTINUOUS surrogate for the
    discontinuous spectral indicator `1_{|t| ≥ r}`. -/
noncomputable def spectralBumpFn (r : ℝ) : ℝ → ℝ := fun t => max 0 (|t| - r)

/-- **r107a.7a: the bump is continuous.** -/
theorem spectralBumpFn_continuous (r : ℝ) : Continuous (spectralBumpFn r) := by
  unfold spectralBumpFn; fun_prop

/-- **r107a.7b: `g_r(0) = 0` for `r ≥ 0`** — the key `f 0 = 0` condition
    that lands the calculus in the NON-UNITAL functional calculus. -/
theorem spectralBumpFn_zero {r : ℝ} (hr : 0 ≤ r) : spectralBumpFn r 0 = 0 := by
  simp only [spectralBumpFn, abs_zero, zero_sub]
  exact max_eq_left (neg_nonpos.mpr hr)

/-- **r107a.7c: the bump is nonnegative.** -/
theorem spectralBumpFn_nonneg (r t : ℝ) : 0 ≤ spectralBumpFn r t :=
  le_max_left _ _

/-- **r107a.7d: `g_r(s) = s − r` for `0 ≤ r ≤ s`** (top of the spectrum). -/
theorem spectralBumpFn_at_pos {r s : ℝ} (hs : 0 ≤ s) (hr : r ≤ s) :
    spectralBumpFn r s = s - r := by
  simp only [spectralBumpFn, abs_of_nonneg hs]
  exact max_eq_right (by linarith)

/-- **r107a.7e: `g_r(-s) = s − r` for `0 ≤ r ≤ s`** (bottom of the
    spectrum) — the symmetric `|·|` makes the bump detect BOTH signed
    norm endpoints, so it works for merely selfadjoint `a`. -/
theorem spectralBumpFn_at_neg {r s : ℝ} (hs : 0 ≤ s) (hr : r ≤ s) :
    spectralBumpFn r (-s) = s - r := by
  simp only [spectralBumpFn, abs_neg, abs_of_nonneg hs]
  exact max_eq_right (by linarith)

/-- **r107a.8: the spectral bump element** `p_r(a) = cfcₙ g_r a` via the
    non-unital continuous functional calculus. -/
noncomputable def spectralBump (r : ℝ) (a : TimelessFieldCompletion) :
    TimelessFieldCompletion :=
  cfcₙ (spectralBumpFn r) a

/-- **r107a.8a: the bump element is selfadjoint.** -/
theorem spectralBump_isSelfAdjoint (r : ℝ) (a : TimelessFieldCompletion) :
    IsSelfAdjoint (spectralBump r a) :=
  cfcₙ_predicate (spectralBumpFn r) a

/-! ## §3 — ★ the reachable heart: the bump element is NONZERO ★ -/

/-- **★★★ r107a.9: NORM LOWER BOUND FOR THE SPECTRAL BUMP ★★★**

    For selfadjoint `a` and `0 ≤ r ≤ ‖a‖`,
    `‖a‖ − r ≤ ‖spectralBump r a‖`.

    Proof: `‖a‖` or `−‖a‖` is a real spectrum point (r107a.6), hence a
    quasispectrum point; the symmetric bump takes value `‖a‖ − r ≥ 0`
    there; and `norm_apply_le_norm_cfcₙ` (the non-unital cfc is
    isometric, so `‖g(s)‖ ≤ ‖cfcₙ g a‖` for `s` in the quasispectrum)
    delivers the bound. -/
theorem norm_spectralBump_ge {a : TimelessFieldCompletion} (ha : IsSelfAdjoint a)
    {r : ℝ} (hr0 : 0 ≤ r) (hr : r ≤ ‖a‖) :
    ‖a‖ - r ≤ ‖spectralBump r a‖ := by
  have hnn : (0 : ℝ) ≤ ‖a‖ := norm_nonneg a
  have hcont : ContinuousOn (spectralBumpFn r) (quasispectrum ℝ a) :=
    (spectralBumpFn_continuous r).continuousOn
  have hz : spectralBumpFn r 0 = 0 := spectralBumpFn_zero hr0
  obtain ⟨s, hs, hval⟩ :
      ∃ s, s ∈ quasispectrum ℝ a ∧ spectralBumpFn r s = ‖a‖ - r := by
    rcases CStarAlgebra.norm_or_neg_norm_mem_spectrum ha with h | h
    · exact ⟨‖a‖, (@spectrum_subset_quasispectrum ℝ TimelessFieldCompletion
        Real.instCommSemiring instCStarAlgebraTimelessFieldCompletion.toRing
        NormedAlgebra.complexToReal.toAlgebra a) h, spectralBumpFn_at_pos hnn hr⟩
    · exact ⟨-‖a‖, (@spectrum_subset_quasispectrum ℝ TimelessFieldCompletion
        Real.instCommSemiring instCStarAlgebraTimelessFieldCompletion.toRing
        NormedAlgebra.complexToReal.toAlgebra a) h, spectralBumpFn_at_neg hnn hr⟩
  have hle : ‖spectralBumpFn r s‖ ≤ ‖spectralBump r a‖ :=
    norm_apply_le_norm_cfcₙ (spectralBumpFn r) a hs hcont hz ha
  rw [hval, Real.norm_of_nonneg (by linarith : (0 : ℝ) ≤ ‖a‖ - r)] at hle
  exact hle

/-- **★★★ r107a.10: THE SPECTRAL BUMP IS NONZERO ★★★**

    For nonzero selfadjoint `a`, `spectralBump (‖a‖/2) a ≠ 0` — indeed
    `‖a‖/2 ≤ ‖spectralBump (‖a‖/2) a‖`. This is Glimm's "cut near the top
    of the spectrum" step, executed with the CONTINUOUS calculus. -/
theorem spectralBump_ne_zero {a : TimelessFieldCompletion} (ha : IsSelfAdjoint a)
    (ha0 : a ≠ 0) : spectralBump (‖a‖ / 2) a ≠ 0 := by
  have hpos : 0 < ‖a‖ := norm_pos_iff.mpr ha0
  have hbound := norm_spectralBump_ge ha (r := ‖a‖ / 2) (by positivity) (by linarith)
  have hlt : 0 < ‖spectralBump (‖a‖ / 2) a‖ := by
    have : ‖a‖ - ‖a‖ / 2 = ‖a‖ / 2 := by ring
    rw [this] at hbound; linarith
  exact norm_pos_iff.mp hlt

/-! ## §4 — PRIORITY 3: the honest reduction + the two named links -/

/-- **★ r107a.11: the honest completion-tier reduction. ★**

    The r106 engine `ideal_trace_ne_zero_forces_top` closes full
    completion simplicity AS SOON AS, in every nonzero two-sided ideal,
    the spectral-bump element (i) lies in the ideal (WALL A) and (ii) has
    nonzero UHF trace (WALL B). Both are supplied here as EXPLICIT
    hypotheses — they are precisely the two mathlib-unreachable links. -/
theorem completion_simple_of_bump_links
    (hlink : ∀ (I : TwoSidedIdeal TimelessFieldCompletion), I ≠ ⊥ →
      ∃ a, IsSelfAdjoint a ∧ a ≠ 0 ∧ a ∈ I ∧
        spectralBump (‖a‖ / 2) a ∈ I ∧
        UHF_trace (spectralBump (‖a‖ / 2) a) ≠ 0) :
    ∀ I : TwoSidedIdeal TimelessFieldCompletion, I = ⊥ ∨ I = ⊤ := by
  intro I
  by_cases hI : I = ⊥
  · exact Or.inl hI
  · obtain ⟨_, _, _, _, hmem, htr⟩ := hlink I hI
    exact Or.inr (ideal_trace_ne_zero_forces_top I _ hmem htr)

/-- **r107a.12: the same links discharge trace-detection** (r106.s), and
    hence (composing with r106.u) completion-tier FAITHFULNESS of τ_UHF. -/
theorem traceDetects_of_bump_links
    (hlink : ∀ (I : TwoSidedIdeal TimelessFieldCompletion), I ≠ ⊥ →
      ∃ a, IsSelfAdjoint a ∧ a ≠ 0 ∧ a ∈ I ∧
        spectralBump (‖a‖ / 2) a ∈ I ∧
        UHF_trace (spectralBump (‖a‖ / 2) a) ≠ 0) :
    SubstrateCompletionTraceDetectsIdeals := by
  intro I hI
  obtain ⟨_, _, _, _, hmem, htr⟩ := hlink I hI
  exact ⟨_, hmem, htr⟩

/-- **r107a.13: faithfulness from the bump links** — chaining r107a.12
    with r106's `UHF_trace_faithful_of_traceDetects`. -/
theorem UHF_trace_faithful_of_bump_links
    (hlink : ∀ (I : TwoSidedIdeal TimelessFieldCompletion), I ≠ ⊥ →
      ∃ a, IsSelfAdjoint a ∧ a ≠ 0 ∧ a ∈ I ∧
        spectralBump (‖a‖ / 2) a ∈ I ∧
        UHF_trace (spectralBump (‖a‖ / 2) a) ≠ 0) :
    ∀ x : TimelessFieldCompletion, UHF_trace (star x * x) = 0 → x = 0 :=
  UHF_trace_faithful_of_traceDetects (traceDetects_of_bump_links hlink)

/-! ## §5 — r107a capstone -/

/-- **★★★ r107a SUBSTRATE SPECTRAL-BUMP + WALL-MAP CAPSTONE ★★★**

    Bundles the reachable r107a content:

      (S1) `exists_selfAdjoint_ne_zero_mem_of_ne_bot` — step (α): a
           nonzero ideal contains a nonzero selfadjoint element.
      (S2) `spectralBumpFn_continuous` + `spectralBumpFn_zero` — the
           concrete continuous bump with `g_r(0) = 0`.
      (S3) `spectralBump_isSelfAdjoint` — the cfcₙ bump is selfadjoint.
      (S4) **`spectralBump_ne_zero`** — the bump element is NONZERO for
           nonzero selfadjoint `a` (continuous spectral cut).
      (S5) **`completion_simple_of_bump_links`** — the r106 engine closes
           simplicity given the two named links (WALL A ∧ WALL B).

    Kernel-only [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]. Zero project
    axioms. Zero sorries.

    Substrate significance: r107a lays the FIRST BRICK toward the r106
    hypothesis `SubstrateCompletionTraceDetectsIdeals`, discharging the
    fully-reachable `a`-side (step α) and the CONTINUOUS spectral-cut
    (step β up to the projection) with mathlib's `cfcₙ`, and pinning the
    exact wall as TWO named links: WALL A (`p ∈ I` needs a
    closed-ideal / Pedersen-ideal + `cfcₙ`-in-ideal API absent from
    mathlib) and WALL B (`τ_UHF(p) ≠ 0` needs discontinuous
    spectral-projection cfc + hereditary-subalgebra/corner + comparison
    of projections, all absent). r107 is thus genuinely gated on new
    mathlib CStar theory, not on a bounded Lean push. -/
theorem r107a_substrate_spectral_bump_capstone :
    (∀ (I : TwoSidedIdeal TimelessFieldCompletion), I ≠ ⊥ →
        ∃ a, IsSelfAdjoint a ∧ a ≠ 0 ∧ a ∈ I) ∧
    (∀ (r : ℝ), Continuous (spectralBumpFn r)) ∧
    (∀ {r : ℝ}, 0 ≤ r → spectralBumpFn r 0 = 0) ∧
    (∀ (r : ℝ) (a : TimelessFieldCompletion), IsSelfAdjoint (spectralBump r a)) ∧
    (∀ {a : TimelessFieldCompletion}, IsSelfAdjoint a → a ≠ 0 →
        spectralBump (‖a‖ / 2) a ≠ 0) ∧
    ((∀ (I : TwoSidedIdeal TimelessFieldCompletion), I ≠ ⊥ →
        ∃ a, IsSelfAdjoint a ∧ a ≠ 0 ∧ a ∈ I ∧
          spectralBump (‖a‖ / 2) a ∈ I ∧
          UHF_trace (spectralBump (‖a‖ / 2) a) ≠ 0) →
      ∀ I : TwoSidedIdeal TimelessFieldCompletion, I = ⊥ ∨ I = ⊤) :=
  ⟨exists_selfAdjoint_ne_zero_mem_of_ne_bot,
   spectralBumpFn_continuous,
   spectralBumpFn_zero,
   spectralBump_isSelfAdjoint,
   spectralBump_ne_zero,
   completion_simple_of_bump_links⟩

